Encode the eap and active_account identity claims.

What: Identity gains eap and active_account (ActiveAccount, AccountStanding,
ClaimTime, all exported). dumps() writes both right after "scopes"; inside
active_account the optional values are written only when set, and valid=False
is still written while an absent verdict is omitted.

Files: iam/__init__.py, iam/_identity.py, iam/_wire.py, tests/test_wire.py.

Why: other services already mint these claims; the codec must emit the same
bytes. Expected values are captured from the issuing implementation, and the
existing full-wire literals were updated for the two new keys. Decoding lands
next, which is what stops forwarded identities losing the claims.

Checks: make check (ruff, taplo, mypy, 850 tests); independent review approved.
